<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balaji Baji Rao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1720–1761</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Nanasaheb Peshwa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balaji Baji Rao, known as Nanasaheb, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> from 1740 to 1761, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baji-rao-i">Baji Rao I</a>. Under him Maratha power reached its widest extent, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and the south, and the Peshwa became the real ruler of the Maratha state. His reign ended in disaster with the defeat at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-battle-of-panipat">Third Battle of Panipat</a> in 1761, and he died a few months later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balaji-baji-rao.jpg" alt="Balaji Baji Rao" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balaji_Baji_Rao.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
